 "notes": "IBS-CAPP haloscope search using tunable TM020 mode, 21.38-21.79 ueV (5.17-5.27 GHz). Curve traced from the red 'This work' region boundary in the inset of Fig. 6 (y-axis |g_agamma/g_agamma^KSVZ| linear scale) of the e-print PNG figure; the frequentist limit (red curve, average 12.0 x KSVZ at 90% CL) was chosen as the main result, not the Bayesian gray region (10.9 x KSVZ). Ratio converted to g_agamma via g_KSVZ = 1.92*(alpha/2pi)/f_a with m_a = 5.7 ueV x (1e12 GeV/f_a), i.e. g_KSVZ = 3.91e-16 GeV^-1 x (m_a/ueV); consistency check: mean of extracted points is 12.1 x KSVZ. Paper assumes rho_a = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (matches canonical, no rescaling). Narrow notch gaps in the excluded region (~21.43, 21.62, 21.76 ueV, mode crossings/vetoed bins) are bridged by binned sampling; vertical edge walls excluded from the trace.",
